lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.5.1-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.0.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M3 Max (Apple9) - Apple M3 Max (14 threads) - 36.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen dragging a not-selected node into the inspector, the inspector stays on the old object (good!) but the tree selection goes to the new object (bad!). This puts the inspector in a confusing state, because what is now selected in the scene tree is not showing in the inspector. To add insult to injury, clicking on the now newly selected object in the tree again also does not select that object in the inspector.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5054634-07e9-4d6f-9069-39265252046d\n\nThe expected behavior is that the selection in the tree returns to the object that is being selected – primarily because that's what the inspector is showing.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSelect an object from the scene tree and drag another object from the tree anywhere. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repit